# Kelwick Marine

## Current Model

**Kelwick Marine** was the vendor of record on the inactive **Pier 9 Single-Contractor Plan** — a unified envelope covering both gate retrofit and gangway replacement with shared mobilization, badge pool, and liability rider. Victor Dunn circulated the **single-contractor plan** at Q2 kickoff while P9-GATE and P9-GANG scopes were still introduced as parallel Pier 9 workstreams. Victor Dunn formally retired the **pier 9 single-contractor** track on **2026-05-06** after scope divergence; **Kelwick Marine** remains named on the old plan for audit trail only while execution moved to Turnstile Dynamics (P9-GATE) and Bridgeway Hoist (P9-GANG).

## Evidence

- `2026-04-20-q2-kickoff-terminal` - Week-1 kickoff notes show P9-GATE and P9-GANG still rolling up under Victor Dunn's **Pier 9 Single-Contractor Plan** with **Kelwick Marine** as vendor of record — single mobilization, shared badge pool, one liability rider covering both gate retrofit and gangway replacement.
- `2026-05-06-single-contractor-superseded` - Victor Dunn formally retired the **pier 9 single-contractor** envelope effective 2026-05-06 citing scope divergence; **Kelwick Marine** remains named on the old **single-contractor plan** for audit trail only while P9-GATE moves to Turnstile Dynamics and P9-GANG to Bridgeway Hoist.

## Use In Work

- Do not quote Kelwick Marine as an active Pier 9 vendor in passenger notices or procurement routing after 2026-05-06 — treat as superseded audit reference only.
- When retrieving Pier 9 vendor history, distinguish the Kelwick single-contractor era (weeks 1–2) from the split-vendor track under the Q2 Terminal Readiness Playbook.

## Limits

Kelwick Marine does not appear on post-split PO tracks, badge batches, or delivery schedules. Derek Blunt's 2026-04-27 vendor-split email already directed gate and gangway quotes to Turnstile Dynamics and Bridgeway Hoist before formal supersession.

## Connections

- [[plan-pier9-single-contractor]] - Inactive plan that named Kelwick Marine as unified Pier 9 vendor.
- [[decision-supersede-single-contractor]] - Decision retiring Kelwick envelope after gate and gangway scope divergence.
- [[victor-dunn]] - Infrastructure program manager who authored and superseded the single-contractor plan.
- [[p9-gate-retrofit]] - Pier 9 gate scope that was under Kelwick before splitting to Turnstile Dynamics.
=== END FILE ===

