# Bridgeway Hoist

## Current Model

**Bridgeway Hoist** is the **P9-GANG** **gangway vendor** — assigned gangway fabrication and hydraulic install after the Pier 9 vendor split. As **p9-gang vendor**, Bridgeway owns the gangway replacement scope on a separate hoist contract and berth window from Turnstile Dynamics. **Gangway delivery** remained firm for **2026-05-21** despite Turnstile gate slip chatter; Derek Blunt confirmed **Bridgeway delivery** details unchanged on 2026-05-14. On arrival day the Bridgeway truck rolled to east apron staging per Victor Dunn's map with berth 9B scheduled gangway AM only.

## Evidence

- `2026-04-27-vendor-split-announcement` - Derek assigns **P9-GANG → Bridgeway Hoist** for gangway fabrication and hydraulic install; **Bridgeway Hoist** owns the **gangway replacement** scope as **p9-gang vendor** on a separate PO track from Turnstile gate work.
- `2026-05-14-gangway-delivery-hold` - Despite Turnstile slip chatter, **gangway delivery** is still firm for **2026-05-21**; **Bridgeway delivery** details unchanged — gate vendor delay does not push gangway because of different hoist contract and berth window.
- `2026-05-21-gangway-arrival-day` - Bridgeway truck on site for **gangway delivery** **2026-05-21** with east apron staging; Marcus enforces contractor shift ban — no back-to-back shifts with Turnstile gate crew on the same Pier 9 berth.

## Use In Work

- Schedule P9-GANG gangway crew windows and load-test prep around the firm 2026-05-21 delivery — do not defer gangway staging because Turnstile slipped to May 28.
- Keep Bridgeway Hoist change orders on the P9-GANG cost code separate from Turnstile Dynamics P9-GATE spend.

## Limits

Bridgeway Hoist does not own P9-GATE fare lane hardware, night lighting commissioning, or gate delivery schedules. Priya Nandakumar still required a gangway load test certificate before passenger boarding tests even after delivery landed.

## Connections

